AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0410171> "Cotinine is the main metabolite of nicotine and accumulates in the body as a result of tobacco exposure. In humans, cotinine is excreted in the urine, mainly as trans-3[prime]-hydroxycotinine and glucuronide. This is used as a measure for exposure to tobacco smoke.")
